      "locator": "Abiotic methods p2030 and Results pp2024-2025",
      "assessment": "Separate oxalic/citric chemical assays use50uL0.05mM acid on slides; agar wells0.1/0.5/0.75M oxalic or0.5/0.75/1M citric; solutions50/100mM acid. These are not a matched quantitative isolation of live-culture acid effects. Citric acid was negative for synthetic-hydroxyvanadinite dissolution in tested conditions."
    },
    {
      "locator": "Methods p2030; Figures4-5",
      "assessment": "Recovered crystals were extracted using80C water and vacuum dried. EDX used carbon tape, acquired before Au/Pd coat to avoid Pb/Cl overlap; therefore a C peak alone is not a phase identity. XRPD methods report3-70degrees2theta and ICDD standards, original pattern missing."
